%% Real time: continuous development with a continuously-thinking architect
sequenceDiagram
  participant OP as OPERATOR
  participant FD as FRONT DESK
  participant AR as ARCHITECT (future)
  participant OR as ORCHESTRATOR
  participant RM as item room (present)
  Note over OR,RM: STEADY STATE — nothing waits for design
  OR->>OR: grounding probe → charter (cites map rows + test verdicts)
  OR->>RM: launch (worktree)
  RM->>RM: SDD: brainstorm-lite reads corpus → plan → build
  RM->>RM: hits arch-vs-code discrepancy → RESOLVES IT LOCALLY<br/>plants a debt MARKER if the clean fix belongs to a later pass
  RM-->>OR: pointer: residue row (discrepancy + marker + insight)
  RM-->>FD: event: "residue filed"
  OR->>OR: collects residue · watches checkpoints (merges, milestones)
  RM->>RM: finishes → FF-CAS merges → retires its own worktree
  AR-->>OR: pointer: conformance report on the published diff (advisory)
  OR->>OR: next charter absorbs markers / follow-up item
  Note over OP,AR: CHECKPOINT → DESIGN SESSION
  OR-->>AR: pointer: checkpoint reached — residue COLLECTION handed over
  AR->>AR: works the collection: clusters, contested rows, marker census, agenda
  AR-->>FD: event: agenda ready
  FD-->>OP: one queue; operator attaches to ARCHITECT
  OP->>AR: session in-room: census-first · lettered forks · rulings
  AR->>AR: update angles + map + D# (supersede, never erase)
  AR-->>OR: pointer: map changed → re-charter / close stale items
